---
title: Lemon bars
servings: 16
yield: 16 squares
tags: [vegetarian]
time: 1 hour 10 minutes
source: Lemon Squares by King Arthur Test Kitchen, King Arthur Baking, https://www.kingarthurbaking.com/recipes/lemon-squares-recipe
---

Heat the oven to 350°F (175°C). Line an #8-inch square pan{} with parchment.

== Crust ==

Whisk the @all-purpose flour{120%g}, @table salt{1/4%tsp} and
@powdered sugar{28%g}. Work in the @unsalted butter{113%g}(room temperature)
until evenly mixed and crumbly.

Press it firmly into the pan. If it sticks to your hands, freeze it 5 to 10
minutes first.

Bake ~{30%minutes} to 35 minutes, until golden brown. Turn the oven down to
325°F (165°C).

== Topping ==

While the crust bakes, whisk the @eggs{4}(large), @egg yolks{1}(large),
@granulated sugar{223%g} and @powdered sugar{21%g} until smooth. Whisk in the
@all-purpose flour{30%g} and @table salt{1/8%tsp}, then the
@lemon juice{152%g}.

Let it stand ~{15%minutes}, until most of the bubbles have gone.

== Bake ==

Pour the topping over the hot crust. Bake ~{30%minutes}, until set and fairly
dry on top.

Cool completely on a #wire rack{} before cutting. Dust with
@powdered sugar{} just before serving.

> Grated zest of a lemon stirred into the crust gives it more lemon. Keep
> leftovers in the fridge 3 to 4 days.
